# Decoded-image memory and resample cost: subsampling for JPEG/WebP/PNG plus a
# cached subimage for repeated downscaled draws.
# Merged from: webkit-skia-image-subsampling, webkit-webp-subsampling,
# webkit-png-subsampling, webkit-cached-subimage.
#
# Upstream gates image subsampling to Apple/CG. Un-gated for USE(SKIA), an image
# displayed smaller than its natural size decodes at 1/2, 1/4 or 1/8 resolution,
# cutting both decode CPU and decoded-bitmap RAM — the RAM-safe way to speed up
# image-heavy pages here (raising the decoded-image cache instead OOMs).
# Min area worth subsampling drops from Apple's 5 MP to ~1 MP
# (WEBKIT_IMAGE_SUBSAMPLE_MIN_AREA) so 1-3 MP feed photos are covered.
#
# Per format:
#  - JPEG: libjpeg IDCT scaling.
#  - WebP: libwebp use_scaling; output dimensions come from
#    scaledSizeForSubsamplingLevel() so they agree with frameSizeAtIndex()
#    (verified at denominators 1-8 incl. odd sizes). Still images only —
#    animated WebP composites frames in full-resolution canvas coordinates.
#    DEVICE-MEASURED (build 579, 40 stills 2000x1500 drawn at 750 device px):
#    settled WebProcess RSS 638 MB -> 278 MB (-361 MB, -56%). Largest single
#    memory win measured on this port.
#  - PNG: libpng has no scaling equivalent, so rows are box-filtered as they
#    arrive through the progressive callback — only the smaller backing store
#    plus ONE accumulator row is ever allocated, so PEAK decode memory drops,
#    not merely the retained copy. The accumulator keeps alpha-premultiplied
#    r,g,b sums plus an alpha sum and a sample count, so dividing by the alpha
#    sum averages AND un-premultiplies in one step. Non-interlaced, non-animated
#    only (Adam7 delivers rows across seven passes via a full-size interlace
#    buffer — no peak win to be had). Verified at denominators 2/4/8 incl.
#    ragged 13x7.
#
# CachedSubimage completes it: upstream ships the class but the two hooks that
# drive it return false with no non-Cocoa override and the driver does not exist
# in the tarball at all, so on WPE every repaint of a downscaled image resamples
# the full-resolution bitmap again. Adds the driver plus a BitmapImage override,
# so a large scaled-down image is rasterized once at display resolution and
# blitted thereafter. Scoped to unrotated, source-over, non-animated, actually
# downscaled draws >= 256x256 of source (WEBKIT_CACHED_SUBIMAGE_MIN_AREA); the
# cache drops on dataChanged()/destroyDecodedData() so memory-pressure pruning
# reclaims it. WEBKIT_CACHED_SUBIMAGE=0 restores stock.
#   DEVICE-MEASURED (build 579, file:// benches with fling paths disabled so the
#   paint path is actually exercised): steady state at scale 0.11 —
#   34.1 -> 44.1 fps (+29%), p95 64 -> 30 ms (-53%), jank 19% -> 2%, Skia raster
#   CPU 43% -> 4.5%. Cold cost is one fill per image per scale.
#   The cache buffer is the DRAWN area, so it costs scale^2 of a decoded frame
#   while saving 1 - scale^2 of the resample — hence the max-scale gate at 0.5
#   (>= 75% of the benefit for <= 25% of a decoded frame);
#   WEBKIT_CACHED_SUBIMAGE_MAX_SCALE=1.0 restores "any downscale".
#
# ---
